也就是说，这四十年里买的衣服，都得适合在办公室穿。

30
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:04,560
So then when we all go to like donate our clothes we just have so many blouses to get rid of.
所以等我们捐衣服的时候，就有特别多衬衫需要清理。

31
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,480
And that's why their thrift stores are like full of them.
这就是旧衣店里到处都是这类衬衫的原因。

32
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:11,919
Really the years that most people are experimenting are in college or like the first few years out of high school.
多数人真正尝试不同穿衣风格的阶段，是大学或者高中毕业后的头几年。

33
00:02:11,919 --> 00:02:17,039
Where there's like no restrictions such as like an office or school dress code.
那时候没有办公室或学校着装规范这样的限制。

34
00:02:17,039 --> 00:02:24,880
So since most experimentation is only happening for like four or 5 years the stuff that's getting donated is only like four or 5 years worth of clothing.
所以如果主要只有四五年在尝试穿搭，后来捐出的，也就只有那四五年积累的这些衣服。

35
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:28,320
Anyway the hunt is what makes thrifting special.
总之，寻找的过程，才让淘衣变得特别。

36
00:02:28,320 --> 00:02:33,120
Like when you find a cute piece it's really like you treasure hunted.
找到一件可爱的衣服，就真的像寻到了宝。

37
00:02:33,120 --> 00:02:36,560
Y'all this is a reformation top.
朋友们，这是一件 Reformation 的上衣。

38
